# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for vendored Aeron client internals.
#
# Aeron's media-driver conductor thread and the application poll thread
# communicate through lock-free ring buffers / log buffers using CPU
# memory-ordering fences (Atomic64_*.h, AtomicBuffer volatile accessors).
# TSan cannot see Aeron's hardware-fence-based happens-before edges, so it
# reports these cross-thread accesses as data races even though they are
# correct by Aeron's C++ memory model. These races live entirely inside the
# vendored `aeron::` library (Image poll / TermReader / AtomicBuffer wrap /
# CopyBroadcastReceiver image creation) and are NOT fixable in rune code.
#
# Scope: only the aeron::concurrent / aeron::Image internal accessors below.
# rune's own replication/HW/log state is NOT suppressed — a real rune-side
# race will still fail the build.

# AtomicBuffer wrap/capacity/volatile reads during Subscription/Image::poll.
race:aeron::concurrent::AtomicBuffer::wrap
race:aeron::concurrent::AtomicBuffer::capacity
race:aeron::concurrent::AtomicBuffer::getInt32Volatile

# Ordered stores/loads on Aeron's log-buffer metadata (fence-based ordering).
race:aeron::concurrent::atomic::putInt64Ordered
race:aeron::concurrent::atomic::putInt32Ordered

# Image::isClosed() atomic bool load racing the conductor's Image construction.
race:aeron::Image::isClosed
race:aeron::Image::poll

# Term reader / header buffer wrap while the conductor rotates term buffers.
race:aeron::concurrent::logbuffer::TermReader::read
race:aeron::concurrent::logbuffer::Header::buffer
race:aeron::concurrent::logbuffer::FrameDescriptor::frameLengthVolatile

# HeaderWriter / ExclusivePublication claim path (client publish vs conductor).
race:aeron::concurrent::logbuffer::HeaderWriter::write
race:aeron::ExclusivePublication::tryClaim
race:aeron::ExclusivePublication::newPosition

# Broadcast receiver image-created callback (conductor publishes new Image).
race:aeron::concurrent::broadcast::CopyBroadcastReceiver::receive

# Subscription image array: the conductor publishes a new array through
# AtomicArrayUpdater (a seqlock whose ordering comes from STANDALONE acquire/
# release fences, which TSan does not model); the polling thread reads it in
# Subscription::poll / imageCount / imageBySessionId.  Aeron-internal.
race:aeron::util::addToArray
race:aeron::util::removeFromArray
# Reader side of the same seqlock: Subscription::imageBySessionId copies a
# shared_ptr<Image> out of the conductor-published image array (refcount bump
# racing the conductor's Image construction) — Aeron-owned memory only; rune
# calls the public single-poller API from the subscription's own poll thread
# (ImageLossWatch::afterPoll).  F27 re-review: confirmed Aeron-internal.
race:aeron::Subscription::imageBySessionId

# Checkpoint A (TSan, rune_auth_cluster_tests): the same two Aeron-internal
# edges reached through the sibling read paths the list above missed.
#  - Image::controlledPoll is Image::poll's controlled twin: it reads the
#    subscriber position and the mmapped log buffer (prior "write" = the
#    conductor's mmap / Image construction).  rune's gateway polls through it.
#  - Image::sourceIdentity / Image::sessionId read fields of an Image the
#    conductor built and published through the AtomicArrayUpdater seqlock;
#    rune reaches them via Subscription::forEachImage on the poll thread
#    (AeronPartitionTransport plane-reconnect scan).
# Function-scoped, Aeron-owned memory only; rune's own state is not covered.
race:aeron::Image::controlledPoll
race:aeron::Image::sourceIdentity
race:aeron::Image::sessionId

# Checkpoint A (TSan): Aeron C's username() (aeron_fileutil.c) fills a function-local `static char static_buffer[16384]`
# through getpwuid_r when $USER is unset; aeron_default_path() calls it from every aeron_context_init /
# aeron_driver_context_init, so two threads building an Aeron context at once (a broker's EmbeddedDriver and a test
# client) race on that buffer.  Aeron-internal and environment-dependent (only without $USER); every Rune context sets an
# explicit aeron.dir, so the default path built from it is overwritten and never used.  Scoped to that one Aeron file.
race:aeron_fileutil.c

# Checkpoint E (TSan, rune_peer_link_agent_tests): the reader of a freshly mapped log buffer.  The prior "write" is
# the client conductor's mmap of the Image's log buffer (MemoryMappedFile::doMapping); the read is a fragment handler
# reached through Image::poll / TermReader::read, whose template frames symbolize without the `aeron::` prefix, so
# the poll entries above do not match.  The mapping's publication to the poller is Aeron's fence-ordered image hand-off.
race:aeron::util::MemoryMappedFile::doMapping
# The client conductor builds an aeron::Image (make_shared) and publishes it to the subscriber thread through Aeron's
# own ordered array store (atomic::putValueOrdered - invisible to TSan); every read of the new Image's fields on the
# polling thread (UnsafeBufferPosition::get, Header::offset, AtomicBuffer::getInt64/boundsCheck, Image::poll inlined
# into the caller's template frame) then reports against that allocation.  Matched on the allocating frame, so it
# covers Aeron's Image hand-off only (TSan CI: WorkerReplicationTransportInteg, PeerSealed*, PeerLinkAgent*).
race:_Sp_counted_ptr_inplace<aeron::Image
# The C client's async add (aeron_client_conductor_async_add_*) hands the command to its conductor through Aeron's
# MPSC command queue (C11 atomics in a different TU than TSan sees ordered); the conductor's memcpy of the command
# body reports against the caller's write (TSan CI: UdpGsoBindings.*).
race:aeron_client_conductor_async_add_
# Same queue, other commands: async_destination (MDS add / remove destination) is copied by the conductor's
# on_cmd_destination (TSan CI: UdpGsoBindings.MdsDestinationRemovedOnTheReceiverIsCounted).
race:aeron_client_conductor_async_destination
# Dedicated threading: the conductor opens a channel's socket and hands the endpoint to the receiver thread through
# the driver's MPSC command queue; TSan's fd tracking then reports the receiver's epoll_ctl against the socket()
# (TSan CI: BrokerNodeTest.DedicatedAeronThreadingMode_BootsAndElects).
race:aeron_udp_transport_poller_add
# The driver's own MPSC command ring (aeron_mpsc_rb_write on one driver agent, aeron_mpsc_rb_read + its memset on the
# other) orders through C11 atomics in the uninstrumented Aeron build; Rune never uses this ring itself
# (TSan CI: BrokerNodeTest.DedicatedAeronThreadingMode_BootsAndElects).
race:aeron_mpsc_rb_
